  "Name": "Young1963-model-4layer",
  "Source": "L. Young, \"Multilayer reflection coatings on a metal mirror,\" Appl. Opt. 2, 445-447 (1963). doi:10.1364/AO.2.000445 - Fig. 1, Fig. 2 inset and Eq. (7), p. 446",
  "Notes": "Computed model of Fig. 2: 4 quarter-wave ZnS/cryolite layers on a fictitious lossless medium of index 132 that has the 97 % reflectance of gold.\nSpecification: Maximum reflectance at the band centre f/f0 = 1.\nReported: Fig. 2 (scale 1): peak R ~0.996 at f/f0 = 1 (plot); Eq. (6): x = 0.6^4 = 0.1296, R ~ 0.9961. Curves symmetric about f/f0 = 1 on a frequency scale and return to the bare-medium R = 0.970 at f/f0 = 0 and 2 (half-wave layers). Text p. 447 (4 layers): f/f0 = 1.156 on scale 1 (Rm = 0.97) gives R = 0.9925. With reference_nm 1000, f/f0 = 1000/lambda(nm).\nNotes: Fig. 1 and the Fig. 2 inset show the stack from the incident medium (n = 1) as ZnS (high, n1) / cryolite (low, n2) / ... / cryolite / metal, i.e. the low-index layer is next to the metal and the high-index layer faces the light; listed here in that order. All layers are quarter waves at reference_nm with non-absorbing constant indices ZnS 2.2, cryolite 1.32. Normal incidence, vacuum/air incident medium. reference_nm 1000 is arbitrary: the paper plots against normalized frequency f/f0 = reference_nm/lambda (0 to 2), so band_nm [500, 4000] covers f/f0 = 0.25-2. Substrate n = 132, k = 0 from Eq. (7) (n = (1+sqrt(Rm))/(1-sqrt(Rm)) for Rm = 0.97). Scale 2 of Fig. 2 corresponds to Rm = 0.982, i.e. an equivalent medium n = (1+sqrt(0.982))/(1-sqrt(0.982)) ~ 220 (not printed).\nLayers from Fig. 1, Fig. 2 inset and Eq. (7), p. 446; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R 0.9933 at f/f0 = 1.156 (865.1 nm); paper R 0.9925 (read from Fig. 2).",
